title The last file at its own body md5, and the two lines a stub took off the meter
prompt The baton and the card -- the card named glow/lower_face.rye as the ident arc's next fall and said it waits for a lap of its own.
rota lap 5371, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop. Standfast asks a line to halt on a known wrong, and the cold run handed me seventeen. Reading them one at a time for my own lane rather than in aggregate is what the row bought: none touches glow/, the two nearest are build-path reds over mycelium/ and a tree-wide ceiling, and the card now says which reds this lap walked past instead of reporting only its own green.
think Checked the claim board before building -- six live claims, none in glow/, verdict clear -- then opened pheromone-lower-face-ident-stub and pushed it before a byte of the build, so a peer could read it.
think Measured the file rather than taking the card's word for it. Its fn zig_safe_ident body differs from the seven landed this morning by exactly one local name, c against ch, md5 e4cec7a4 against 049cce28 -- and it is the last file standing at that md5.
think The stub is the room's landed idiom: same out type, same LowerError name, a new field slice so the refusal record reads field=gate rather than field=face, a u32 return where the copy answered usize, delegating to zig_ident.safe_ident.
think Each of the 29 call sites takes the hyphenated name of the thing it lowers, derived from the call's own first argument -- mix-left, jam-right, subject -- so a refusal names which face refused.
think Measured the width delta rather than the state: copied my file aside, checked out the inherited bytes, ran the scan, restored. 1145 to 1143 corpus lines; files unmoved at 277.
obs The file stays flagged because five usize struct fields remain in BoundValue -- cast_mold_len and four subject*_len -- across 37 in-file sites. lower_named_cast.rye already carries that same field at u32 with the @intCast idiom, so the migration is written and unclaimed; left out of this lap to keep one keystone.
obs Read the fifteen remaining copies by body md5 and declared ceiling, and wrote the reading into the scan's own ceiling comment rather than only into the card -- three max_arm_len siblings at 31 sites each, a rm.max_name_len pair at 14 and 15, nine singletons, and lower_alias the one body that is genuinely a different rule since it maps the dot.
